      'When Tars stops without being quit (a crash, a power cut, a restart of your Mac), the agents that were working start again on their own conversation at the next launch, a few at a time, with a note from Tars: when it stopped, what was cut (the command that was running), that their background tasks stopped, and to check before redoing anything. Their last request is not sent again. Agents that were at rest stay asleep until something needs them. What Tars still owed an agent, the note that an agent it handed work to has finished, a room message or a Kanban note, is kept on disk where no agent can write it, and given at its first rest after the restart, said to be from before it and sent by Tars.',
